Package: easyDR
Title: Dose-Response Meta-Analysis, Made Teachable
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Vanio", "Antunes", email = "vanio.antunes.md@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A front end for dose-response meta-analysis, argued like the
    'meta' package. One call takes a long table of exposure categories and a
    summary measure such as "RR" or "SMD", derives the contrasts and the
    within-study covariances, pools them, and reports the pooled
    dose-response with its heterogeneity, prediction interval and predicted
    effects. Companion plots cover the curve, a forest of study trends,
    leave-one-out, meta-regression with bubble plots, and a funnel with
    Egger's test. Estimation is delegated to 'dosresmeta'. Built alongside
    the free book at <https://vanioljantunes.github.io/easyDR/>.
